    "fig3_roc_auc": 0.6281452000000001,
    "claim_verdict": "Across both datasets and every input-level runtime variant tried (STRIP \u03b1\u2208[0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9], a class-conditioned threshold, the `replace` and validity-preserving `marginal` perturbations, and the Ma et al. benign-conversion-rate baseline), TPR@5%FPR never exceeds 0.072, so no simple input-level runtime detector reaches a usable operating point on this all-to-benign backdoor. Two qualifications: (1) a weak ranking signal remains: the best AUC is 0.827, and on the measured entropy distributions triggered inputs have lower entropy than clean-benign inputs (ROC-AUC 0.628), i.e. they are not cleanly separable at a usable FPR; (2) the failure is operational (at a usable FPR), not a strict impossibility of any input-level signal. Screening-level Neural Cleanse remains the effective detector for this threat."
  }
